# HeroUI Native UI

- For UI elements, prefer components from `heroui-native` before creating custom primitives.
- Use project/local components only when they wrap or compose `heroui-native`, or when `heroui-native` does not provide the needed primitive.
- Do not add a new UI library without explicit approval.
- Keep screen-specific layout in React Native/Uniwind classes, but shared interactive UI such as buttons, inputs, labels, spinners, and form fields should come from `heroui-native`.
- Uniwind-ограничения и эталон карточек списка: `.cursor/rules/uniwind-styling.mdc`.

read the docs "my-master-react-native/.heroui-docs"
